<%# Fuime: the parent's first email is the pitch (ONBOARDING_PLAN §4.2). It
    says why now, what they are agreeing to, and what their signature gates.
    Every sentence branches where merchant-of-record and Connect differ:
    under MoR the signature gates PAYOUTS; under Connect it gates ACTIVATION.
    It promises nothing the product does not do — no "important
    notifications", no tax summary (neither mailer exists), and the
    no-SSN / no-ID / no-payment line is stated only under MoR, where
    GuardianshipsController#accept is a checkbox and the payout destination is
    collected later; under Connect, Stripe's onboarding does ask (L3). %>
<p>
  Hi —
</p>

<p>
  <strong><%= @minor_name %></strong> just set up
  <% if @venture_name.present? %>
    <strong><%= @venture_name %></strong>
  <% else %>
    a business
  <% end %>
  on Fuime, a financial platform for young founders. Because they're under 18,
  a parent or guardian has to be the responsible adult on the account, and
  <%= @minor_name %> named you.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>What you're agreeing to</strong> <em>(one page, about two minutes)</em>
</p>

<ul>
  <li>You're the legal signer for <%= @venture_name.presence || "their business" %>. <%= @minor_name %> runs it day to day.</li>
  <li>You can see every sale and every dollar, always. <%= @minor_name %> can't turn that off.</li>
  <% if @merchant_of_record %>
    <%# Not "until you approve it": payouts run as a weekly Fuime::PayoutBatch a
        Fuime admin approves, and a scheduled line has no teen request for the
        parent to decide. What the parent's acceptance and destination set-up
        gate is whether money can go out at all (Event#payout_setup_blockers). %>
    <li>Nothing is paid out until you've accepted and set up where the money goes.</li>
  <% else %>
    <li>Nothing goes live until you accept.</li>
  <% end %>
</ul>

<p>
  <% if @merchant_of_record %>
    <%# "Keep going", not "take orders": selling under MoR waits on Fuime's human
        vetting (Fuime::OperatorEligibility), and this email usually fires on
        application submit, before that decision. The parent is not what holds
        the teen up; that is all this sentence may claim. %>
    <%= @minor_name %> can keep going without waiting on you.
    <strong>They can't be paid until you sign.</strong>
  <% else %>
    <strong><%= @minor_name %> can't run it until you sign.</strong>
  <% end %>
</p>

<p>
  <%= link_to "Review and sign", @accept_url,
              style: "display:inline-block;background:#2242FF;color:#ffffff;padding:12px 20px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:8px;font-weight:600;" %>
</p>

<p style="word-break: break-all;">
  Or paste this link into your browser:<br>
  <%= link_to @accept_url, @accept_url %>
</p>

<p>
  <% if @merchant_of_record %>
    We won't ask for a Social Security number, an ID, or a payment. When
    there's money to send, we'll ask where it should go.
  <% else %>
    Accepting is free and doesn't ask for an ID. Before any money moves,
    Stripe will need identity details from the account owner.
  <% end %>
</p>

<p>
  Not expecting this? Ignore it — nothing happens unless you accept.
</p>

<p>
  Questions? Reply to this email or write to <%= @support_email %>.
</p>

<p>
  Thanks,<br>
  The Fuime team
</p>
